## Git workflow

- Work in your own worktree (`git worktree add`), never in the shared checkout.
- Branches: `<type>/<issue>-<slug>`. Commits: Conventional Commits, `type(scope): subject`.
- Squash-merge only; the PR body carries `Fixes #N`.
- Stage explicit paths by name — never `git add -A`, `.`, `-u`, `<dir>/`, or `commit -a`.
- Assert the branch (`git branch --show-current`) before the first edit and before staging.

## Review & merge gate

The default risk tier is MEDIUM. The self-merge posture is pinned in
`.claude/skill-profile.md` (`### Self-merge posture`) and nowhere else. Never
`gh pr merge --admin` and never `--auto`: the `main` ruleset has no bypass actors.

## CI

One required check: `ci-gate`, which needs every job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and
fails on any failure or cancellation. Jobs run where the `route` job sends them: a fork PR
goes to hosted runners; otherwise the `runner_mode` dispatch input, then a head-commit title
tag (`[github]`, `[macos]`, `[windows]`, `[linux]`), then `vars.RUNNER_DEFAULT`, then
`["self-hosted","macOS","ARM64"]`. There is no skip tag and no automatic fallback to hosted.

